y", "start": 258.075, "end": 258.45}, {"text": "platforms", "start": 258.45, "end": 259.4}, {"text": "solve", "start": 259.4, "end": 259.775}, {"text": "this", "start": 259.775, "end": 260.025}, {"text": "with", "start": 260.025, "end": 260.212}, {"text": "self", "start": 260.212, "end": 260.875}, {"text": "service", "start": 260.875, "end": 260.875}, {"text": "config", "start": 260.875, "end": 261.675}, {"text": "and", "start": 261.675, "end": 261.825}, {"text": "GitOps", "start": 261.825, "end": 262.275}, {"text": "workflows", "start": 262.275, "end": 263.15}]}, {"index": 20, "kind": "prose", "text": "There's also a philosophical split: centralized gateways (one team, one config) vs. sidecar/decentralized approaches where each service owns its edge via something like Envoy. Large orgs often end up with both — a thin edge gateway for auth and DDoS protection, plus per-service sidecars for fine-grained policy.", "start": 263.4, "end": 284.175, "words": [{"text": "There's", "start": 263.65, "end": 263.825}, {"text": "also", "start": 263.825, "end": 264.2}, {"text": "a", "start": 264.2, "end": 264.3}, {"text": "philosophical", "start": 264.3, "end": 265.0}, {"text": "split", "start": 265.0, "end": 265.7}, {"text": "centralized", "start": 265.7, "end": 266.525}, {"text": "gateways", "start": 266.525, "end": 267.387}, {"text": "one", "start": 267.387, "end": 267.675}, {"text": "team", "start": 267.675, "end": 268.25}, {"text": "one", "start": 268.25, "end": 268.7}, {"text": "config", "start": 268.7, "end": 269.15}, {"text": "vs", "start": 269.15, "end": 269.625}, {"text": "sidecar", "start": 269.625, "end": 270.925}, {"text": "decentralized", "start": 270.925, "end": 270.925}, {"text": "approaches", "start": 270.925, "end": 271.525}, {"text": "where", "start": 271.525, "end": 271.712}, {"text": "each", "start": 271.712, "end": 271.962}, {"text": "service", "start": 271.962, "end": 272.425}, {"text": "owns", "start": 272.425, "end": 272.662}, {"text": "its", "start": 272